+### pi.invokeExtensionCommand(name, args?) (Familiar downstream)
+
+```typescript
+const command = pi.getCommands().find(c => c.source === "extension" && c.name === "review:2");
+if (command) await pi.invokeExtensionCommand(command.name, "unchanged args");
+```
+
+Invokes only an exact registered extension command (including collision suffixes),
+with a fresh command context. No leading slash, built-ins, skills, templates,
+input event, or model turn. Args default to `""` and are passed unchanged.
+The promise resolves after completion; unknown names, stale/uninitialized runtimes,
+busy sessions, any active awaited runner event dispatch, the entire agent_settled
+method, and nested or concurrent public invocations reject. Handler Errors retain
+identity; other thrown values become `Error(String(value))`. Await/catch errors;
+programmatic invocation does not also emit an extension error event.
+
+The owning AgentSession must be idle and outside its `agent_settled` dispatch
+at admission. `ctx.isIdle()` retains upstream semantics (true during that event). Active
+run tools/events cannot cross into command-only session controls: waiting there
+can deadlock on the caller itself (upstream commit `0d9fddec`, issue #2023).
+One runner-local public-invocation slot excludes even A -> B: different commands still
+mutate the same session. Calls reject rather than queue. The slot is released
+in `finally`, including handler failures and successful runtime replacement.
+Old captured pi/ctx remain stale after replacement or reload.
+
+This API is for an idle external human frontend, not deferred scheduling or a
+session-wide lock. Hosts must still gate other session actions during the handler.
+`AgentSession.prompt()` is unchanged: direct handlers, immediate dispatch even
+while streaming, overlap, context creation, and error reporting retain upstream
+behavior. It neither acquires nor checks the public API slot. Hosts must coordinate
+prompt/public concurrency. Public calls reject while runner event dispatch is active,
+including idle shutdown, before-switch/fork, compaction/tree, startup/reload and
+resource/input/provider pipelines. No other idle lifecycle callbacks are admissible.
+A runner-local depth spans each complete awaited emitter, including early returns
+and throws; it does not serialize events or lock unrelated non-event actions.
+The public API has no bypass option.
+
+Do not use a follow-up user message as a command queue. In 0.85.1,
+`sendUserMessage` defaults to literal model-visible text; its `expandPromptTemplates`
+opt-in is void, parses text, expands skills/templates, and dispatches commands before
+streaming queueing. It does not replace this awaited idle-only API.
+
 ### pi.getCommands()
 
 Get the slash commands available for invocation via `prompt` in the current session. Includes extension commands, prompt templates, and skill commands.
